---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { FAMILIES } from '../../lib/circle';
import '../../styles/circle.css';
---
<Layout title="Know your keys" description="Memorise a chord family on the circle of fifths, then fill in its missing names and numbers.">
  <a class="back-link" href="/">← All exercises</a>
  <section class="keys" data-circle aria-labelledby="keys-title">
    <div class="keys-heading">
      <div><p class="keys-kicker">THE CHORD FAMILY TRAINER</p><h1 id="keys-title">Know your keys.</h1></div>
      <label class="family-picker">Chord family
        <select id="family">{FAMILIES.map(([major, minor], i) => <option value={i}>{major} major / {minor} minor</option>)}</select>
      </label>
    </div>
    <div class="key-toolbar">
      <div class="key-modes" role="group" aria-label="Choose the home key">
        <button id="major-key" type="button" aria-pressed="true">C major</button>
        <button id="minor-key" type="button" aria-pressed="false">A minor</button>
      </div>
      <span id="mode-note">Same chords. A different home.</span>
    </div>
    <div class="trainer">
      <figure class="circle-figure">
        <svg id="family-circle" viewBox="0 0 600 600" role="img" aria-labelledby="circle-title circle-description">
          <title id="circle-title">C major chord family</title>
          <desc id="circle-description">Six chords and their scale numbers in fixed circle-of-fifths positions.</desc>
          <circle class="orbit" cx="300" cy="300" r="242"/>
          <circle class="orbit inner-orbit" cx="300" cy="300" r="155"/>
          <g id="circle-guides" aria-hidden="true"></g>
          <g id="circle-chords"></g>
          <text id="circle-home" class="circle-home" x="300" y="290" text-anchor="middle">C major</text>
          <text class="circle-centre-caption" x="300" y="318" text-anchor="middle">CHORD FAMILY</text>
        </svg>
        <div id="diminished" class="diminished" hidden></div>
        <figcaption>Major chords outside · minor chords inside<br/><span>The circle stays still. Only the numbers change.</span></figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div class="trainer-content">
        <div class="round-progress"><span id="round-label">FIRST, LOOK AT THE PATTERN</span><span id="round-count"></span></div>
        <div id="round-dots" class="round-dots" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <h2 id="prompt" tabindex="-1">Six chords. One shape.</h2>
        <p id="instruction" class="trainer-instruction"></p>
        <div id="study-pattern" class="study-pattern"></div>
        <div id="choices" class="trainer-choices" role="group" aria-label="Choose your answer" hidden></div>
        <p id="feedback" class="trainer-feedback" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
        <div class="trainer-actions">
          <button id="primary" type="button" class="trainer-primary">Try a round →</button>
          <button id="hint" type="button" class="trainer-text" hidden>Peek at the pattern</button>
          <button id="secondary" type="button" class="trainer-text" hidden>Study again</button>
        </div>
        <p id="learning-note" class="learning-note"></p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <details class="keys-help" id="key-help">
      <summary>About numbers &amp; alternate key names</summary>
      <p>A number tells you which scale note a chord is built on. The chord name tells you its quality: Am is minor; Bdim is diminished. In Roman numerals, major chords use uppercase and minor chords use lowercase.</p>
      <p>Major pattern: outer <strong>4–1–5</strong>, inner <strong>2–6–3</strong>. Natural-minor pattern: outer <strong>6–3–7</strong>, inner <strong>4–1–5</strong>. Read each arc anticlockwise to clockwise around the highlighted family.</p>
      <p>The bottom of the circle has shared positions: <strong>B = C♭, F♯ = G♭, C♯ = D♭</strong>. Their relative minors are G♯m/A♭m, D♯m/E♭m and A♯m/B♭m. The exercise always uses the spelling that belongs to your key.</p>
      <p>After you can recall and rebuild the six-chord family, you’ll add the diminished chord: number 7 in major, number 2 in natural minor. Minor here means natural minor, with a minor chord 5.</p>
    </details>
    <p id="storage" class="storage-note" role="status"></p>
    <noscript><p>Enable JavaScript to use the chord family trainer.</p></noscript>
  </section>
</Layout>
<script src="../../scripts/circle.ts"></script>
